{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786281609,"nonce":"ILn9dFxgGSBp6nKpGvkdIttURag=","message":"Fixed in 994e334. It was worse than filed: golangci-lint was not installed on this machine at all, and BOTH the wrapper and `rtk proxy golangci-lint run ./...` exited 0 while doing nothing — so `just lint` reported success with no linter present, not merely with a mis-parsed argument.\n\n`just lint` now invokes the binary by absolute path (`$(go env GOPATH)/bin/golangci-lint`) and treats its absence as fatal. `just setup` tests for it by path rather than with `command -v`, which the wrapper answers for. The Makefile named in the ticket no longer exists — `just` is the only runner as of ADR 0021.\n\nRunning it for the first time: **0 depguard violations**, so the layering rules the ticket was worried about did hold. It did find 7 real issues in test files added this week (4 govet unusedwrite, 2 revive unused-parameter, 1 staticcheck), all fixed in the same commit. Two of the unusedwrite cases were tests asserting less than they set up, so they were fixed by asserting the rest rather than by deleting the fields.\n\nReady to close.","files":null}]}